**~80%**. Treat that as a rough estimate, not something this CFTC table identifies: it reports futures positions but not the offsetting cash Treasury holdings. The New York Fed put basis-trade estimates at roughly $600 billion–$1 trillion against more than $1 trillion in leveraged-fund net shorts across Treasury futures up to 10 years in March 2025, which supports about 80% as a midpoint. ([New York Fed](https://www.newyorkfed.org/newsevents/speeches/2025/per250509), [CFTC analysis](https://www.cftc.gov/sites/default/files/Basis_trade_Mixon_Orlov_ada.pdf))